<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Che Guevara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1928–1967</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ernesto Guevara, Ernesto Che Guevara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernesto 'Che' Guevara was an Argentine-born Marxist revolutionary, a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-revolution">Cuban Revolution</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a> and later a minister in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>. Seeking to spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war, he fought in the Congo and in 1966 went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, where his small band failed to win peasant support. He was captured by the Bolivian army on 8 October 1967 and executed the next day at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-higuera">La Higuera</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/che-guevara.jpg" alt="Che Guevara" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alberto Korda, restored by Adam Cuerden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Che_Guevara_-_Guerrillero_Heroico_by_Alberto_Korda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
